# The library asks `$findsDeclaredMember(this, "has")` in order to go by what it knows of its own function. "The function under the name is library code" does not say that.
# A NAME ON A PROTOTYPE IS UNMARKED ONLY WHERE THE BODY OF A FILE LAYS IT: a body takes no `this` and no arguments, so nobody brings it the prototype or the value:
# the body of a file of the library, whatever it stores; the body of a file of the program, where the store spells the function: that function is the program's, and the walk refuses it by its role.
# "has": the store stands in the class's own file, ANOTHER FILE BRINGS THE FUNCTION . "laid": a function of the library writes the function at the store, THE PROGRAM BRINGS THE PROTOTYPE (Readable.prototype.wrap)
# "copied": a function of the library copies what the program brings (util._extend) . "own": written at the store in the body of the class's file . "destroy": the library's own body stores what it reads off its own record
